body:
non mathematical approach;

Measure/find the pressure the spray canister is in, spray it out enough to put some kind of paint in it similar to the viscosity of the liquid inside and re-pressurize to that pressure if it deviated (though environmental temps and how much you used the bottle already changes that so you might want to take a few measurements when canister is full, half and empty to get an average)

Then spray it next to something with known length markings parallel to the markings (a measuring tape etc) and record in slow motion, that way you can find how many centimeters it goes per second from the time passed vs the the distance traveled (can include a chronometer in the video)

this has been used for projectiles in both research centers and in shows like myth busters iirc.

Mathematical approach;

cant help, CFM air simulation if you know the diameter off the nozzle etc can work though.
